# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Setup {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import the libraries used throughout the tutorial and fix a random seed for reproducibility.\n"
msgstr "Impor library yang dipakai sepanjang tutorial dan tetapkan random seed supaya hasilnya reproduksibel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator skala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start with eight assets drawn from six sectors and select exactly $K=4$ of them. With only eight assets there are only $\\binom{8}{4}=70$ valid portfolios, so we can later check the quantum result against an exhaustive search.\n"
msgstr "Kita mulai dengan delapan aset dari enam sektor dan memilih tepat $K=4$ di antaranya. Dengan hanya delapan aset, hanya ada $\\binom{8}{4}=70$ portofolio valid, sehingga nanti kita bisa memeriksa hasil kuantum terhadap pencarian menyeluruh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each asset is one qubit; a bitstring like `10110010` is a portfolio (the 1s are the assets we hold). We need three ingredients: the market data, the three objective Hamiltonians, and a circuit that only ever proposes portfolios with exactly $K$ assets.\n"
msgstr "Setiap aset adalah satu qubit; bitstring seperti `10110010` adalah sebuah portofolio (angka 1 adalah aset yang kita pegang). Kita butuh tiga bahan: data pasar, tiga Hamiltonian objektif, dan circuit yang hanya pernah mengusulkan portofolio dengan tepat $K$ aset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Enforcing \"exactly K assets\" without a penalty.** A common trick is to add a penalty term that punishes portfolios of the wrong size, but that couples every qubit to every other qubit, which leads to much deeper circuits after transpilation. Instead we use an **XY mixer**, which only ever moves the QAOA state *between* bitstrings of the same Hamming weight. If we start in a state that already has $K$ assets selected, every portfolio the circuit explores also has exactly $K$ assets. The constraint is built into the circuit's structure rather than enforced by a penalty term.\n"
msgstr "**Menegakkan \"tepat K aset\" tanpa penalti.** Trik yang umum adalah menambahkan suku penalti yang menghukum portofolio dengan ukuran salah, tetapi itu mengopel setiap qubit dengan setiap qubit lain, yang menghasilkan circuit jauh lebih dalam setelah transpilasi. Sebagai gantinya kita memakai **mixer XY**, yang hanya memindahkan state QAOA *di antara* bitstring dengan Hamming weight yang sama. Kalau kita mulai dari state yang sudah punya $K$ aset terpilih, setiap portofolio yang dijelajahi circuit juga punya tepat $K$ aset. Batasan ini tertanam di struktur circuit, bukan ditegakkan lewat suku penalti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare the starting state cheaply: rotate each qubit so it is \"on\" with probability $K/N$. Restricted to the $K$-asset outcomes, this reproduces the ideal equal-weight (Dicke) state, so we simply keep the measured bitstrings that have exactly $K$ ones — a step called *post-selection*.\n"
msgstr "Kita menyiapkan state awal dengan murah: putar setiap qubit sehingga \"menyala\" dengan probabilitas $K/N$. Dibatasi pada hasil dengan $K$ aset, ini mereproduksi state berbobot sama yang ideal (state Dicke), jadi kita cukup menyimpan bitstring hasil pengukuran yang punya tepat $K$ angka satu — langkah yang disebut *post-selection*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi di hardware kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before running, the abstract circuit is transpiled into hardware-native gates. At this small scale we only inspect the cost: how deep is the circuit and how many two-qubit gates does it use? (Two-qubit gates are the main source of noise on real devices.)\n"
msgstr "Sebelum dijalankan, circuit abstrak ditranspile menjadi gate native hardware. Pada skala kecil ini kita hanya memeriksa biayanya: seberapa dalam circuit-nya dan berapa banyak gate dua-qubit yang dipakainya? (Gate dua-qubit adalah sumber utama noise di device nyata.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Jalankan dengan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two stages. First we **train** the QAOA angles once, using equal objective weights, with an exact statevector simulator to find good $\\beta,\\gamma$ values. Then we **sweep** many weight vectors across the simplex and sample the circuit at each, collecting candidate portfolios. Because only the objective weights change between sweeps (not the trained angles), all the weight vectors are submitted in a single batched job.\n"
msgstr "Dua tahap. Pertama kita **melatih** sudut QAOA sekali, dengan bobot objektif yang sama, memakai simulator statevector eksak untuk menemukan nilai $\\beta,\\gamma$ yang bagus. Lalu kita **menyapu** banyak vektor bobot di seluruh simpleks dan men-sampling circuit di tiap titik, mengumpulkan portofolio kandidat. Karena hanya bobot objektif yang berubah di antara sapuan (bukan sudut hasil pelatihan), semua vektor bobot dikirim dalam satu job batch.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We keep only the feasible portfolios (exactly $K$ assets from the post-selection step), score each one on all three objectives, and extract the **Pareto front**: the portfolios that are not beaten on every objective at once. The *hypervolume* is a single number summarizing how much objective space the front dominates, and bigger is better.\n"
msgstr "Kita hanya menyimpan portofolio yang layak (tepat $K$ aset dari langkah post-selection), menilai masing-masing pada ketiga tujuan, dan mengekstrak **front Pareto**: portofolio yang tidak dikalahkan pada semua tujuan sekaligus. *Hypervolume* adalah satu angka yang merangkum seberapa besar ruang objektif yang didominasi front, dan makin besar makin baik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With 100,000 shots over only 256 bitstrings, this run sees every one of the 70 valid portfolios, so at this size it is effectively a brute-force check that the pipeline is wired correctly, rather than evidence that QAOA found the front.\n"
msgstr "Dengan 100.000 shot atas hanya 256 bitstring, run ini melihat ke-70 portofolio valid semuanya, jadi pada ukuran ini ia pada dasarnya adalah pemeriksaan brute force bahwa pipeline terpasang dengan benar, bukan bukti bahwa QAOA menemukan front tersebut.\n"

