msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-approximate-multi-objective-optimization/extracted-outputs/9ccde65a-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh hardware skala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the same workflow on **40 assets** (8 sectors × 5), choosing $K=6$. Forty qubits is too large to simulate exactly (a $2^{40}$-amplitude statevector), so the angles can't be optimized the way they were at eight assets, and a dense circuit would be too deep for current hardware. The $\\binom{40}{6} \\approx 3.8$M valid portfolios are still few enough to enumerate classically, which we use at the end as an exact benchmark. Several things change, and **nothing else about the method does**:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang workflow yang sama pada **40 aset** (8 sektor × 5), memilih $K=6$. Empat puluh qubit terlalu besar untuk disimulasikan secara eksak (statevector dengan $2^{40}$ amplitudo), jadi sudutnya tidak bisa dioptimalkan seperti pada delapan aset, dan circuit yang padat akan terlalu dalam untuk hardware saat ini. Sebanyak $\\binom{40}{6} \\approx 3.8$M portofolio valid masih cukup sedikit untuk dienumerasi secara klasik, yang kita pakai di akhir sebagai tolok ukur eksak. Beberapa hal berubah, dan **tidak ada hal lain dari metodenya yang berubah**:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Train the angles with a matrix-product-state (MPS) simulator, not exact statevector.** Following the reference (Kotil et al.), we fix the objective weights to equal values, optimize a single β, γ on the MPS simulator, and reuse them for every weighting vector in the sweep. (We train at the size we run — no small-to-large angle transfer.)\n"
msgstr "**Latih sudut dengan simulator matrix-product-state (MPS), bukan statevector eksak.** Mengikuti referensi (Kotil et al.), kita menetapkan bobot objektif sama, mengoptimalkan satu β, γ di simulator MPS, dan memakainya ulang untuk setiap vektor pembobotan dalam sapuan. (Kita melatih pada ukuran yang kita jalankan — tanpa transfer sudut dari kecil ke besar.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sparsify the risk model to fit hardware.** A full covariance couples all 780 asset pairs. We keep only the strongest, cheapest-to-route couplings using *importance-aware QAP truncation*, and couple each sector in a light ring for the diversity term. This keeps the objectives meaningful while holding the circuit to a hardware-friendly size.\n"
msgstr "**Jarangkan model risiko agar muat di hardware.** Kovarians penuh mengopel semua 780 pasangan aset. Kita hanya menyimpan kopling terkuat yang paling murah di-routing dengan *pemangkasan QAP yang sadar-kepentingan*, dan mengopel setiap sektor dalam cincin ringan untuk suku diversitas. Ini menjaga tujuan tetap bermakna sambil menahan circuit di ukuran yang ramah hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Keep the circuit shallow and score honestly.** Routing is stochastic, so we transpile with several seeds and keep the shallowest (and no quantum time is spent). Portfolios are always **scored against the true, full objectives**. The sparsification only shapes the circuit, not how portfolios are judged.\n"
msgstr "**Jaga circuit tetap dangkal dan nilai dengan jujur.** Routing bersifat stokastik, jadi kita mentranspile dengan beberapa seed dan menyimpan yang paling dangkal (dan tidak ada waktu kuantum yang terpakai). Portofolio selalu **dinilai terhadap tujuan penuh yang sebenarnya**. Penjarangan hanya membentuk circuit, bukan cara portofolio dinilai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Why QAP truncation?\">\n"
"Keeping each asset's largest couplings by magnitude alone can result in a circuit that is sparse but still awkward to route. QAP truncation instead keeps couplings that are both large *and* physically close on the chip, so the same gate budget buys a shallower, more hardware-friendly circuit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Kenapa pemangkasan QAP?\">\n"
"Menyimpan kopling terbesar tiap aset berdasarkan magnitudo saja bisa menghasilkan circuit yang jarang tetapi tetap sulit di-routing. Pemangkasan QAP justru menyimpan kopling yang besar *dan* dekat secara fisik di chip, sehingga anggaran gate yang sama menghasilkan circuit yang lebih dangkal dan lebih ramah hardware.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map inputs (sparsified for hardware) {#step-1-map-inputs-sparsified-for-hardware}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input (dijarangkan untuk hardware) {#step-1-map-inputs-sparsified-for-hardware}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 2-3: train the angles, then build and submit the hardware job {#steps-2-3-train-the-angles-then-build-and-submit-the-hardware-job}"
msgstr "Langkah 2-3: latih sudut, lalu bangun dan kirim job hardware {#steps-2-3-train-the-angles-then-build-and-submit-the-hardware-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Forty qubits is too large to optimize the angles exactly, so we train one $\\beta, \\gamma$ on a\n"
"matrix-product-state simulator at equal objective weights and reuse them across the sweep.\n"
"The cell below loads pre-trained values from a file. The trained cost-layer angle is small\n"
"($\\gamma \\approx 0.32$), so the circuit applies a gentle bias rather than a sharp projection.\n"
msgstr ""
"Empat puluh qubit terlalu besar untuk mengoptimalkan sudut secara eksak, jadi kita melatih satu $\\beta, \\gamma$ di\n"
"simulator matrix-product-state pada bobot objektif yang sama dan memakainya ulang di seluruh sapuan.\n"
"Sel di bawah memuat nilai hasil pelatihan dari sebuah file. Sudut lapisan biaya hasil pelatihan kecil\n"
"($\\gamma \\approx 0.32$), jadi circuit menerapkan bias lembut, bukan proyeksi tajam.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process into the Pareto front and read off the optimal portfolios {#step-4-post-process-into-the-pareto-front-and-read-off-the-optimal-portfolios}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses menjadi front Pareto dan baca portofolio optimalnya {#step-4-post-process-into-the-pareto-front-and-read-off-the-optimal-portfolios}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this problem size, QAOA performs about as well as uniform random sampling. Both recover a large fraction of the exact optimum's hypervolume, and neither is clearly ahead. This outcome is expected for a single shallow QAOA layer with a heavily truncated cost operator on noisy hardware; the value of this example is the end-to-end multi-objective workflow (mapping, angle training, constrained sampling, and Pareto post-processing), not a quantum speed-up. Narrowing the gap to the optimum would call for deeper circuits (more QAOA layers), a gentler truncation, or lower-noise hardware.\n"
msgstr "Pada ukuran masalah ini, QAOA berkinerja hampir sama baiknya dengan sampling acak seragam. Keduanya memulihkan sebagian besar hypervolume optimum eksak, dan tidak ada yang jelas unggul. Hasil ini wajar untuk satu lapisan QAOA dangkal dengan operator biaya yang dipangkas besar-besaran di hardware yang noisy; nilai contoh ini ada pada workflow multi-objektif ujung-ke-ujung (pemetaan, pelatihan sudut, sampling terbatas, dan pasca-proses Pareto), bukan pada percepatan kuantum. Mempersempit selisih dengan optimum akan membutuhkan circuit yang lebih dalam (lebih banyak lapisan QAOA), pemangkasan yang lebih lembut, atau hardware dengan noise lebih rendah.\n"

